// Reality: the reality bubble and its levels of detail, and what they mean
// for every agent (REALITY.md).
//
// Cut points, for every agent, as built (REALITY.md steps 3 and 4):
// - full:     it perceives what happens around it, and decides when it wakes.
// - reduced:  it perceives only what it takes part in (`senses: "own"`), and
//             its own wakes (forgetting, a promise due, hunger's band, a
//             fading trace) wait for the cadence's beat (`every`); what it
//             does runs at full pace.
// - abstract: as reduced, until abstract progression is built
//             (DETAIL_REGIMES.md).
// - frozen:   it neither perceives nor decides, and its activities wait.
//             Risen, its activities are told, and it looks and decides at
//             once.
// - contact:  an event between something at full detail and something not
//             (`contact`'s kinds) raises the other to full while the lease
//             runs.
// - domains:  air, heat, water, light, traces and the body's going without
//             run over the whole world at every level of detail, frozen
//             included: they don't yet step by region.
// - progressions: what a thing does by itself as time passes is a topic's
//             to declare (#Rate, #Turn, in the `progressions` family), and
//             runs alike at every level of detail, frozen included. The
//             other forms (an approach, a periodic operation, a change of
//             grain) and regimes are not built (DETAIL_REGIMES.md).
// - code:     src/core_reality.odin (anchors, levels, leases), core_wakes.odin (the
//             cadence); src/domains_progressions.odin applies every
//             progression: its horizon is the next one due, its wake then.

// The reality bubble (REALITY.md): how exactly each part of the world is
// simulated, by how far it is from what anchors it. Four levels of detail:
// full, reduced, abstract, and, beyond them all, frozen. With no anchors at
// all, the whole world is full.
//
// A kind of anchor says, for each level, how far it reaches: `across`, in
// chunks (32 tiles) on its own level, any direction; `up` and `down`, in
// levels. An anchor's centre is the chunk it stands in, and moves only
// when it has gone `margin` tiles past that chunk's edge, so an anchor
// walking along an edge doesn't bring the world up and down with each step.
#Reach:      { across: int & >=0 & <=4096, up: *0 | int & >=0 & <=63, down: *0 | int & >=0 & <=63 }
#AnchorKind: { full: #Reach, reduced: #Reach, abstract: #Reach, margin: *4 | int & >=0 & <=31 }

// A player, or whatever the game follows as closely.
player:  #AnchorKind & { full: { across: 1, up: 1, down: 1 }, reduced: { across: 4, up: 2, down: 2 },
                         abstract: { across: 16, up: 4, down: 4 } } @family(anchors)
// Something watched from afar: a siege, a story's other thread.
distant: #AnchorKind & { full: { across: 0 }, reduced: { across: 2 }, abstract: { across: 8, up: 1, down: 1 } }
@family(anchors)

// Contact: an event between something at full detail and something not
// raises the other to full, while the lease it gives runs; the events that
// count, and how long after the last of them.
#Contact: { kinds: [...text], lease: time & >=0ms & <=1d }

contact: #Contact & { kinds: ["said", "struck", "arrested", "moved"], lease: 60s } @family(contact)

// What runs at a level below full (REALITY.md step 3): its agents' senses,
// "all" (what happens around them) or "own" (only what they take part
// in: their own doings, what is done to them); and the cadence, `every`,
// that the times they would wake by themselves (to forget, to grow
// hungry, to keep a commitment) are put off to, so that far off they don't
// each make a boundary of their own. Below reduced, as reduced, until
// abstract and frozen have ways of their own.
#Level: { senses: *"all" | "own", every: *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=1d }

reduced: #Level & { senses: "own", every: 10s } @family(levels)

// A progression (DETAIL_REGIMES.md decisions 4 and 5): what a thing does by
// itself as time passes, read in closed form, never stepped. It `progresses` a
// component (its name: "Patch"), and reckons from a time the component
// keeps (`asOf`, a field's name), in periods the component gives (`period`,
// a field's name too, so that each blueprint has its own).
#Progression: { progresses: text, asOf: text, period: text }

// A rate: the field that `rises` is `risesBy` more each period, up to the bound
// the field `upTo` holds. At its bound it rests, its time 0; found below
// its bound with no time, its time is then (what took it below needn't
// say so).
#Rate: #Progression & { rises: text, risesBy: *1 | int & >=1 & <=1000000, upTo: text }

// A turn: the field `turned`, standing `turnedFrom`, stands `turnedTo` one
// period after its time. What set it to stand so set its time.
#Turn: #Progression & { turned: text, turnedFrom: text, turnedTo: text }
